{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For</b> — a parable: like dry stubble, fully dry, with drunken men. Fire comes and consumes everything in a single moment. Now <i>sir'im</i> [thorns] tangled is from the root of 'held fast in a thicket' [נאחז בסבך]." "And the word <i>sevu'im</i> [intoxicated ones] — an adjective, in the manner of השכוני באהלים (Genesis 27:29) [i.e., a stative/passive formation]; also עצום וארוך [the form is both forceful and elongated]." "וכסבאם — when they drink." "<b>They were consumed</b> — they were burned together in fire while they were tangled one with another, like <i>sir'im sevukhim</i> [thorns tangled], and they were tangled in their drunkenness; then they are easy to burn in fire together, like fully dry stubble, because of the extreme dryness of the thorns and the heat of drunkenness. Now he gave a parable from water and from fire, and all this is on account of the king of Nineveh, who exiled Israel and plotted to destroy the remnant of Judah — and this is it."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:34.654030243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}